This package contains the `<%= ctx.network.name %>` network of the `<%= ctx.serviceName %>` OpenWS contract (version <%= ctx.version %>), generated by `openws-sdkgen`. Each network ships as its own package so it can be versioned and evolved independently. Do not edit the generated files by hand — they are overwritten on the next generation.

## Installation

Install `<%= ctx.packageName %>` with the Unity Package Manager, e.g. as a local or embedded package, or from your registry via `Packages/manifest.json`:

```json
{
    "dependencies": {
        "<%= ctx.packageName %>": "<%= ctx.version %>"
    }
}
```

The `com.unity.nuget.newtonsoft-json` dependency is resolved automatically.

## Consuming the generated library

The package ships two assemblies: `<%= ctx.network.assemblyName %>` (the generated code) and `<%= ctx.network.userAssemblyName %>` (an `.asmref` folder whose `partial` handler stubs compile into the SDK assembly).

1. Reference `<%= ctx.network.assemblyName %>` from your own `.asmdef`, or place your code inside `Runtime/<%= ctx.network.userAssemblyName %>`.
2. Import the generated namespaces, create the network, wrap it in a `Runtime`, and connect. See the example below.
3. Handle incoming messages by subscribing to the generated `On<Message>` events, or by implementing the `partial Handle<Message>` stubs in `<%= ctx.network.userAssemblyName %>`.

